  "claim": "The character played by an actor in this film series, in which Anna Shaffer played the role of Ruby Button, was the founder of the Order of the Phoenix. This actor was in a play 'Otherwise Engaged' from 1976 through 1981.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Michael Gambon. Sentence: Gambon has played the eponymous mystery writer protagonist in the BBC television serial \"The Singing Detective\", Jules Maigret in the 1990s ITV serial \"Maigret\", and Professor Albus Dumbledore in the final six \"Harry Potter\" films after the death of previous actor Richard Harris.\nPage: Albus Dumbledore. Sentence: As part of his backstory, it is revealed that he is the founder and leader of the Order of the Phoenix, an organisation dedicated to fighting Lord Voldemort.\nPage: Otherwise Engaged. Sentence: Michael Gambon took over from Bates in 1976, \"playing it for a year, eight times a week.\"\nPage: Anna Shaffer. Sentence: Anna Shaffer (born 15 March 1992) is an English actress, best known for her roles as Ruby Button in teen soap opera \"Hollyoaks\" and Romilda Vane in the \"Harry Potter\" film series.",
