        "original_id": "f54fae4d-db95-5a8a-9dcf-0b4546ad2c16",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Gambon, Albus Dumbledore, Richard Harris, Anna Shaffer\n- Works: The Singing Detective, Maigret, Harry Potter, Otherwise Engaged, Hollyoaks\n- Organizations: BBC, ITV, Order of the Phoenix\n- Characters: Jules Maigret, Professor Albus Dumbledore, Lord Voldemort, Ruby Button, Romilda Vane\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Michael Gambon took over from Bates in Otherwise Engaged and played the role for a year, eight times a week.\n- Michael Gambon played the mystery-writer protagonist in the BBC television serial The Singing Detective.\n- In the 1990s, Michael Gambon played Jules Maigret in the ITV serial Maigret.\n- After Richard Harris died, Michael Gambon played Professor Albus Dumbledore in the final six Harry Potter films.\n- In Albus Dumbledore's backstory, Albus Dumbledore is revealed to be the founder and leader of the Order of the Phoenix.\n- The Order of the Phoenix is an organisation dedicated to fighting Lord Voldemort.\n- Anna Shaffer was born on 15 March 1992 and is an English actress.\n- Anna Shaffer is best known for playing Ruby Button in the teen soap opera Hollyoaks and Romilda Vane in the Harry Potter film series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7c45dc9e-0a87-51c4-b64f-849ea5628a51",
        "text": "Page: Michael Gambon. Sentence: Gambon has played the eponymous mystery writer protagonist in the BBC television serial \"The Singing Detective\", Jules Maigret in the 1990s ITV serial \"Maigret\", and Professor Albus Dumbledore in the final six \"Harry Potter\" films after the death of previous actor Richard Harris.\nPage: Albus Dumbledore. Sentence: As part of his backstory, it is revealed that he is the founder and leader of the Order of the Phoenix, an organisation dedicated to fighting Lord Voldemort.\nPage: Otherwise Engaged. Sentence: Michael Gambon took over from Bates in 1976, \"playing it for a year, eight times a week.\"\nPage: Anna Shaffer. Sentence: Anna Shaffer (born 15 March 1992) is an English actress, best known for her roles as Ruby Button in teen soap opera \"Hollyoaks\" and Romilda Vane in the \"Harry Potter\" film series.",
